Woodsfolk. A governor and city guards represent imperial authority, but the original gazetteer stresses the inhabitants’ independence. Snowy country, mines, forests and older underground ruins surround the city. [1, 2, 3]</p><h2>The search for the Princess</h2><p>Zak comes to Ingos to find one of the surviving Joons. Court rivalries, Karansul’s schemes and the displaced Green Clan complicate the search. The imprisoned <a href=\"wiki://character/deva\">Lu-a-Jalla</a> is found in the mines, while <a href=\"wiki://character/magess\">Diera</a>’s jealousy helps explain her disappearance. Lu-a-Jalla’s account then sends Zak onward to Suslanger. [4, 5, 6]</p><h2>Sources</h2><p>Based on the original game dialogue and world descriptions. Source numbers refer to the scenes listed below.</p><table data-columns=\"2\"><tr><th>#</th><th>Sources</th></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>World description · Ingos (allod ingos)</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>World description · City environs (zone gz11k)</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>World description · Abandoned mines (zone gz12k)</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>Dialogue · <a href=\"wiki://character/rick\">Tka Rik (Tka-Lithan Richti-Nik)</a>, <a href=\"wiki://character/hero\">Zak</a> (briefing r36)</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>Dialogue · <a href=\"wiki://character/deva\">Lu-a-Jalla</a>, <a href=\"wiki://character/hero\">Zak</a> (briefing d55)</td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td>Dialogue · <a href=\"wiki://character/rick\">Tka Rik (Tka-Lithan Richti-Nik)</a>, <a href=\"wiki://character/hero\">Zak</a>, <a href=\"wiki://character/deva\">Lu-a-Jalla</a> (briefing r54)</td></tr></table><h2>Inhabitants</h2><table data-columns=\"1\"><tr><th>Related page</th></tr><tr><td><a href=\"wiki://character/merc9\">Brissen</a></td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"wiki://character/magess\">Diera</a></td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"wiki://character/vor\">Flein the Baldie</a></td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"wiki://character/ycf\">Grey Leaf</a></td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"wiki://character/shopper\">Karansul</a><